      'A scene behind everything that moves and answers the pointer and a press over the desk. It pours ink into a grid of tones, two samples to the pitch each way, and names one of four inks for each sample. The grid is drawn through one of two filters. Dots: one dot to the pitch, as wide as the ink under it is strong, so two full dots touch. ASCII: a cell is one pitch wide and two high, and its sign is the one of the mono face whose shape fits the ink best; Bouquet sets its own. In colour each dot or sign is in the ink of its place, at the strength of muted. Without colour everything is in the paper ink, at the strength of a line; on a light surface that is the ink of the theme. A scene is laid out on the size of its screen and on the pitch, and a change of either starts it afresh. It runs at 30 frames a second, and stops while the tab is hidden or the desk covered. Under reduced motion and under pause it is drawn once and holds still. A plain wallpaper is not drawn. Passage: dragonflies come in at the bottom left and leave at the top right, the near ones larger, faster and stronger, and each moves aside for the pointer. Bouquet: stems fan out of one point low on the right, twelve flowers of five kinds on them in orange, paper and blue, and between them eight buds and twenty-six sprigs in mint. It turns slowly, and a drag turns it. Forty-six sparks stand behind it and do not turn with it: each keeps its place, drifts a few pixels and twinkles. In signs each kind is made of signs of its own, as hand-made ASCII is, and what is nearer covers what is farther: a round bloom is a block of 0 about an O, a daisy rays of - \\ | / about an @, a tulip a cup of ( | ) with petal tips inside its rim, an allium a ball of * and ., a spike o8o up the end of its stem; a bud is a knot of o, a stem / | \\ by its slope and : where it runs behind, a sprig + and :, a spark . + *. In dots they are poured as ink: a disc with a heart, eight petals about a heart, a cup with two tips, a ball of small spots, discs up the end of a stem. Koi: five, seen from above, wander the screen, the body following the head in a curve, in a coat of white, orange and black patches; without colour the orange is a tone darker. While the pointer is over the desk each swims round it on a ring of its own. Dragonflies: five hover, trembling in place, then dart to a new place in a third of a second and land softly, six times in ten near the pointer; their bodies are orange, blue and mint. Contours: the level lines of a slow relief about a point low on the right, fading toward its edge; every fourth line is heavier, as on a map, and in colour orange. The pointer raises a hill under it. Catfish: three, seen from above, cross from one corner to another on a curved way, barbels trailing and fins paddling, the largest strongest and the smallest faintest; near the pointer one swims three times as fast. Catfish has no colours. Pond: rain on still water, by the wave equation on the pitch. A drop falls now and then, more often near that point low on the right. The pointer leaves a wake as it moves, and a press is a stone whose ring reaches the edge of the screen. Pond has no colours.',
